{title: The LORD Is My Shepherd}
{subtitle: Psalm 23}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Bb]LORD is [Eb]my shepherd
I [Gm]lack nothing
He [Eb]lets me lie down in green [Bb]pastures
He leads me beside [Eb]still waters
He restores my [Gm]soul
He [Eb]guides me along right [F]paths
For his name's [Eb]sake
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Even though I [Bb]walk through the valley of [Eb]the shadow of death
I fear [Gm]no evil, for you [F]are with me
Your rod and your [Eb]staff, they comfort me
You set [Gm]a table before me in [Bb]the presence of my enemies
[Gm]You anoint [Eb]my head with [Bb]oil
My cup over[Fsus4][F]flows
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Surely [Eb]goodness and mercy will pur[Bb]sue me
All the [Eb]days of my life
And I will [Gm]dwell in the [F]house of the [Eb]LORD
For length of [Bb]days [Eb][Gm][F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I will [Eb]dwell in the [F]house of the [Gm]LORD
For length of [Bb]days [Eb][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
